invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_limb.h
catches: p256_equiv_test_sum
reason: the 128-bit form of the subtract with borrow computes
  2^64 + a - b - borrow, whose bit 64 is set when the subtraction did
  not borrow, and returns that bit as the borrow out without inverting
  it. So a chain borrows where it must not and does not where it must,
  and the conditional subtraction after every product keeps the wrong
  value. bin/p256_equiv_test_sum runs this form and holds every
  difference on it to p256_field.c's and p256_scalar.c's.

--- old
    *borrow = (uint64_t)(difference >> 64) ^ 1U;
--- new
    *borrow = (uint64_t)(difference >> 64);
